  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the probabilities of the maximum outcomes (2400 in A with 100%, 2500 in B with 33%) and prefers the lottery with the lower such probability (B). The individual does consider that B offers a higher possible outcome (2500) and acknowledges the low probability of zero, but does not reference or reason about the probability of achieving the maximum outcome in either lottery. The justification is more aligned with risk acceptance and upside potential rather than a deliberate comparison of the likelihoods of the maximum outcomes. Therefore, while the individual chooses B—consistent with the decision reason—the reasoning process described does not align with the specific logic of the decision reason. There is no evidence that the probability of the maximum outcome was a factor in the deliberation.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
